{
  "space": "Money",
  "description": "Household money in six tables. Accounts holds where money sits (checking, savings, cards, cash). Every purchase or payment is a Transaction on an Account, filed under a Category and a Month; every paycheck or refund is an Income row. Bills lists what recurs, with its Monthly cost normalised from any billing period. Months totals what was spent and earned against that month's Budget. Start by adding your Accounts and Categories, then log Transactions as they happen.",
  "icon": "lucide:wallet",
  "tables": [
    {
      "name": "Accounts",
      "description": "One row per place money sits: a checking account, a savings account, a credit card or cash. Spent and Received total the Transactions and Income linked to the account since it was added.",
